LGPL compliance (applies to every published firmware binary)

  The firmware image statically links the LGPL libraries above. To let users
  relink it with modified versions of those libraries, every binary release
  is accompanied by the complete corresponding source of this directory at the
  release tag, including platformio.ini with the exact library versions, so
  the image can be rebuilt with "pio run -e esp32dev" and installed over USB
  or OTA. Devices are never locked against installing a modified image (no
  secure boot, no flash encryption). Release bundles include LICENSE, this
  NOTICE, and the licence texts of the linked components (LGPL-2.1, LGPL-3.0
  together with GPL-3.0, Apache-2.0 and the ESP-IDF component licences).
  Source stays available for at least three years after the last binary
  release.
